<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0980c9feecca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Sleeping Tesla Driver Highlights Autopilot's Biggest Flaw" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ad05b44f038> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla on autopilot drove drunk sleeping man, CA cops say" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1026" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/13ac6e1dcf3e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Officers said they suspect the autopilot feature of the car was being used, the Chronicle reports." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1026" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1456f59cbd36> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His grey Tesla Model S was going 70 miles per hour in a 65 zone." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1026" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/15b58f789cfa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Drunk Tesla Driver Tells Cops Autopilot Was in Charge" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1034" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/17d8f9aaf400> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "CHP: Drunk driver slept while Tesla appeared to drive Hwy 101 on autopilot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/18635e2daae1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Alexander Samek had allegedly dozed off while operating his Tesla Model S when an officer tried to pull him over." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1022" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/19312fbcf0b1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1028] The car was a Tesla Model S, which can be driven on Autopilot, a mode that offers a certain degree of self-driving functionality." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1028" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/22c6f5506f71> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police Catch Tesla Autopilot Driving Home Sleeping Drunk" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1015" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2661a77a90e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The brilliant way cops pulled over a drunk driver passed out in a Tesla on autopilot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1023" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/28353c362050> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Drunk Tesla driver caught asleep behind the wheel at 70mph" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1016" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2d065a7be20d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police Pull Over Self-Driving Tesla with Sleeping Man Behind the Wheel" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1013" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/32399db58ac6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police in the San Francisco Bay Area took an unusual approach to stop a Tesla operating on Autopilot as a drunk driver slept behind the wheel" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1012" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4257922eb0f1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police in the Northern California town of Redwood City arrested a man they found sleeping behind the wheel of his Tesla Model S as it drove down a highway early Friday morning." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1012" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42d8deff1200> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When u pass out behind the wheel on the Bay Bridge with more than 2x legal alcohol BAC limit and are found by a CHP Motor." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1025" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44f3c5f00918> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Some have taken advantage of the situation to criticize Tesla Autopilot — and, by extension, the Advanced Driving Assistance Systems (ADAS) available in many other vehicles — claiming that it encourages people to drive under the influence." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1014" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/451ac4a11ca7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Assuming that the car was on Autopilot, police drove in front of Samek and \"began slowing directly in front of the Tesla in hopes that the 'driver assist' feature had been activated and the Tesla would slow to a stop as the patrol vehicle came to a stop,\" the arrest report said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4cc041481f52> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1022] The Model S is thought to have been in Autopilot, Tesla's semi-autonomous driving mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1022" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4dea70a50db3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1010] Officers observed Samek’s gray Tesla Model S around 3:30 a.m. as it sped south at 70 mph on Highway 101 near Whipple Avenue, said Art Montiel, a CHP spokesman." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/58d09e80e973> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police may have used Tesla’s Autopilot feature to stop driver asleep at the wheel" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1029" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/644af9c11178> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Late last week, a Tesla driver fell asleep in his car around 5:30 p.m. on San Francisco’s Bay Bridge." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/654aeed5890c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Officers observed Samek’s gray Tesla Model S around 3:30 a.m. as it sped south at 70 mph on Highway 101 near Whipple Avenue, said Art Montiel, a CHP spokesman.",
        "Officers observed Samek’s gray Tesla Model S around 3:30 a.m. as it sped south at 70 mph on Highway 101 near Whipple Avenue, said Art Montiel, a CHP spokesman. When officers pulled up next to the car, they allegedly saw Samek asleep, but the car was moving straight, leading them to believe it was in autopilot mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6d070c3f73a7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cops Chased a Tesla for 7 Miles While the Driver Apparently Slept" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1028" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6d8554097298> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It’s possible that the driver may have had another Tesla Model 3 feature on, like Traffic Aware Cruise Control, which manages speed against the car in front of the Tesla." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1029" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6de7fb6a3f45> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla on Autopilot drove 7 miles with driver drunk asleep, police says" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1033" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6f3b250ec558> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a follow-up tweet, Musk said that Autopilot could not distinguish between different types of emergency vehicles, but that it would be able to in the near future." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7401eea1d3ca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"We're adding police car, fire truck & ambulance to the Tesla neural net in coming months,\" he wrote." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/748701b3aa1d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We think that while this may or may not be true (and we hope to see the integration of a driver-focused camera as is used in Cadillac’s Super Cruise which can tell if a vehicle operator is alert and watching the road), it is still, overall, a safety benefit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1014" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/771cef6c0ba4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Redwood City Area CHP officers said they observed Alexander Joseph Samek, a local Los Altos politician, driving at around 3:30 a.m. PST on Nov. 30." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7ac887cd7f10> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1011] For a while, drivers even could buy an Autopilot Buddy “nag reduction device,” until the feds sent the company a cease-and-desist letter this summer." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/884b5b2b0129> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cadillac’s Super Cruise includes a gumdrop-sized infrared camera on the steering column that monitors the driver’s head position: Look away or down for too long, and the system issues a sharp beep." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8a103ab4f884> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last week, when a couple of California Highway Patrol officers spotted a man apparently sleeping in the driver’s seat of a Tesla Model S going 70 mph down Highway 101 in Palo Alto around 3:30 am, they moved behind the car and turned on their siren and lights." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c2d58e2b7b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cops struggle to pull over allegedly drunk, sleeping Tesla driver" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1022" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98cf18346259> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Audi’s Traffic Jam Pilot does the same with an interior gaze-monitoring camera." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/99350ae29ff3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1016] In July 2018, the UK car safety body Thatcham Research called out the “deeply unhelpful” names that some car makers give their driver aids, and highlighted systems such as Tesla’s Autopilot for potentially “lulling drivers into a false sense of security”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1016" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/99bceff006c8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Watch How Cops Use Tesla Autopilot To Stop Alleged Drunk Driver" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1014" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9ab01bebe4c5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1010] The car was a Tesla, the man was a Los Altos planning commissioner, and the ensuing freeway stop turned into a complex, seven-minute operation in which the officers had to outsmart the vehicle’s autopilot system because the driver was unresponsive, according to the CHP." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9ad2e66d610e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "he tried to get out of trouble by claiming that his Tesla was on Autopilot, the vehicle’s proprietary, but still in-development, autonomous driving technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9e3ab305f1d1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver, according to CHP, claimed the car had been “set on autopilot” in an apparent attempt to defend himself." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1034" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a843c531cf90> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1011] For a while, drivers even could buy an Autopilot Buddy “nag reduction device,” until the feds sent the company a cease-and-desist letter this summer." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/afd9fe3c6f71> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Drunk Driver in Tesla Tells Police Officer the Car Was on Autopilot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b3730a3144d3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Model 3 comes with an interior camera mounted near the rearview mirror, and though the automaker hasn’t confirmed what it’s for, don’t be surprised if an over-the-air software update suddenly gives those cars the ability to creep on their human overlords." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bed17b3e1fcc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California Highway Patrol chased a grey Tesla S for an unfathomable seven miles down Highway 101 as the driver slept, police said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c37768897780> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1011] Last week, when a couple of California Highway Patrol officers spotted a man apparently sleeping in the driver’s seat of a Tesla Model S going 70 mph down Highway 101 in Palo Alto around 3:30 am, they moved behind the car and turned on their siren and lights." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c8173c52d628> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A California Highway Patrol officer spotted the Tesla Model S driver out for the count along a highway south of San Francisco." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1016" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c97458fc23e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1030] Cadillac's Super Cruise system would not have allowed you to behave this way because Super Cruise does something that Tesla doesn't do and should do. It has sensors look at your head to see which way it's pointed to make sure your chin's up and not down against your shirt, and also looks at your eyeballs to see where they're looking." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb90d2077fd0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police chased the 'unresponsive' driver of a Tesla S that was on Autopilot for 7 miles in California. How can that happen?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cdec7fe42e98> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Tesla Model S driver was pulled over and arrested by the California Highway Patrol yesterday after the police officers saw him seemingly sleeping at the wheel." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1033" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dfe533054004> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Sleeping Driver's Tesla Led Police On A 7-Minute Chase" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1024" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e6054cd84042> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Drunken driving suspect tells cops his Tesla was on autopilot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1025" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ea38a06bf2f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The car was a Tesla, the man was a Los Altos planning commissioner, and the ensuing freeway stop turned into a complex, seven-minute operation in which the officers had to outsmart the vehicle’s autopilot system because the driver was unresponsive, according to the CHP." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eb1b5d92be53> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla did not confirm that the driver had actually engaged the autopilot system, though it has in the past used driver data in accident investigations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1034" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f21d5aba7c21> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1011] Last week, when a couple of California Highway Patrol officers spotted a man apparently sleeping in the driver’s seat of a Tesla Model S going 70 mph down Highway 101..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe74d61ca2da> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Montiel said officers believed the Tesla was operating on Autopilot because the driver, Alexander Samek, did not respond to their lights and sirens when they tried to pull the vehicle over." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1012" .

