<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/78934dce7f22> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It has sensors look at your head to see which way it's pointed to make sure your chin's up and not down against your shirt, and also looks at your eyeballs to see where they're looking." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9451e4776545> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The car was a Tesla Model S, which can be driven on Autopilot, a mode that offers a certain degree of self-driving functionality." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1028" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0f98d180547b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Redwood City CHP is familiar with the Tesla Autopilot feature in part because of a fatal crash the agency investigated in March." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/227f37589b72> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A 38-year old engineer at Apple died after he did not place his hands on the wheel in time when the car was in Autopilot mode, Tesla said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5b85b6ad6c52> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dan Edmunds, director of vehicle testing at Edmunds, an automotive research firm, has been reviewing partially automated vehicles, and called Tesla’s Autopilot a misleading term for an \"overhyped automated cruise control system.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/807d25114fad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Hopefully a self-driving car would be operating safely enough not to draw the attention of law enforcement,” Christopher Coble, an attorney, wrote in a blog post, “but if you’re pulled over while drunk in an autonomous vehicle, it’s probably going to be on you.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c9bab578dc6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“The combined effects of human error and the lack of sufficient system controls resulted in a fatal collision that should not have happened,” NTSB Chairman Robert Sumwalt said at the time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aaf42adf7e56> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The March crash is being investigated by the National Transportation and Safety Board." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ab26e8593869> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last year, a National Transportation Safety Board investigation into the 2016 death of an Ohio man whose Tesla hit a semi-truck while Autopilot was engaged concluded that Tesla bore some of the blame." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b303f158d1e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Reached by phone Friday afternoon, Samek, a real estate developer who runs the Kor Group, said, “I can’t talk right now,” before hanging up." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c06d345b2817> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "John Simpson, privacy and technology project director with Consumer Watchdog, saw Friday’s incident as further evidence of Tesla drivers being inappropriately led to believe the autopilot function is akin to fully autonomous driving." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce452c618401> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText """Electrek’s Take
First of all, great job by the police here.""" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1033" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e06dfbd31420> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But on Sunday night, Musk tweeted: \"Default Autopilot behavior, if there’s no driver input, is to slow gradually to a stop & turn on hazard lights. Tesla service then contacts the owner. Looking into what happened here.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e62f57c0ee2b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It took California Highway Patrol seven minutes to pull over a Tesla driver." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1022" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ebc82ce5f04e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Australia’s National Transport Commission brought up the question of whether or not automated vehicles should change drunk driving laws last year, as Inverse previously reported." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ebf83a129b0c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But if Autopilot did allow a slumbering and allegedly drunk driver to speed down the highway, it brings up another question: Is Elon Musk’s car company doing enough to prevent human abuse of its technology?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f4b5e22bf55e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The electric luxury sedan had been travelling south on Highway 101, going about 70 mph, California Highway Patrol Officer Art Montiel told Business Insider." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1012" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b8f0d70149f6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Local media reported that cops then had to bang on the window to rouse the driver, who was later identified as Los Altos planning commissioner Alexander Samek." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1028" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dcaea5d14071> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla CEO Elon Musk addressed the situation on Twitter (tweet embedded below), reiterating how the car should behave under Autopilot and saying that he is looking into this particular situation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1014" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9aefd6d6851f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Redwood City California Highway Patrol stopped a Tesla Model 3 they suspected was running Autopilot with a drunk driver asleep at the wheel." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1029" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9f20217df3b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In July 2018, the UK car safety body Thatcham Research called out the “deeply unhelpful” names that some car makers give their driver aids, and highlighted systems such as Tesla’s Autopilot for potentially “lulling drivers into a false sense of security”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1016" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b01de56bdf1a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For a while, drivers even could buy an Autopilot Buddy “nag reduction device,” until the feds sent the company a cease-and-desist letter this summer." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb80bc1adb0a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cadillac's Super Cruise system would not have allowed you to behave this way because Super Cruise does something that Tesla doesn't do and should do." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1030" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d37117604a5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver, 45-year-old Alexander Samek, was drunk and had passed out on his way home." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1013" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/83c4f42411e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That man was 45-year-old Alexander Samek, a Los Altos planning commissioner, and he was drunk." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1015" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c2af5043cc1a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The highway patrol, seemingly unimpressed, arrested the unnamed driver, charged him with suspicion of driving under the influence, and towed his car, noting on Twitter that “no it didn’t drive itself to the tow yard.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1034" .

