<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/73e53f52b8a1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California Highway Patrol officers said they noticed 45-year-old Alexander Samek of Los Altos napping in the driver’s seat around 3:30 a.m." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1026" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/810f71cf6161> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In May, Simpson’s organization and the Center for Auto Safety asked the Federal Trade Commission to investigate “deceptive and unfair” practices in the advertising and marketing of the autopilot feature." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8fff1c1fe408> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "All of which makes the design of similar systems offered by Cadillac and Audi look rather better suited to the task of keeping human eyes on the road, even as the car works the steering wheel, throttle, and brakes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1011" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e8407eab5c92> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Samek, who runs a multi-billion-dollar real estate outfit, The Kor Group, was contacted by SFGate on Friday, but refused to talk to reporters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1014" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3260f4d76909> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver was Alexander Samek, the chair of the Los Altos Planning Commission, according to Palo Alto Online." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1033" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a4b940c5dd8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "CHP public information officer Art Montiel told the LA Times that “there was no training for the situation the officers encountered and attributed the outcome to their ‘quick thinking.’”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1029" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d317d77ffff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla declined to comment on the incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1012" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/05a309aa004e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla declined to comment on the incident, but John Simpson, privacy/technology project director for Consumer Watchdog, calls this proof that Tesla has wrongly convinced drivers their cars' \"autopilot\" function really could perform fully autonomous driving." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1024" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/92ee9afbe363> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Model S is thought to have been in Autopilot, Tesla's semi-autonomous driving mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1022" .

